{{Quote|That place&hellip; is strong with the dark side of the Force. A domain of evil it is. In you must go.''"<br />"''What's in there?''"<br />"''Only what you take with you.|Yoda and Luke Skywalker|<ref name="Episode V" />}}
The '''Cave of Evil''', also known as the '''dark-side cave''', was a large and living [[Dark side of the Force|dark side]] [[vergence]] located under a [[gnarltree]] on the [[swamp]] [[planet]] of [[Dagobah]]. Entering the cave subjected entrants to the vergence's control, projecting their worst fears as apparitions and illusions.

==Description==
[[File:Dagobah_Vergence_FDNP.png|thumb|left|250px|The cave was buried within the swamps of Dagobah]]
The [[Dark side of the Force|dark side]] [[cave]] of [[Dagobah]] was an overgrown landform deep within the endless [[swamp]]s of the forgotten [[Planet|world]]. Little [[Star|sun]] ever reached the surface of the planet, due to the thick canopy, therefore shrouding the cave in an endless twilight. Beneath the thick overgrowth of vines and brambles, ancient stone steps and walls could be seen at one entrance, while a second natural entrance opened in the void<ref name="NoP">''[[Nexus of Power]]''</ref> of a [[gnarltree]] known as The Magic Tree.<ref name="BMF 20">{{BuildFalconCite|20|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> The [[vergence]] that manifested in [[the Force]] within the cave was intense and fueled by the dark side aspects of the universal energy field.<ref name="NoP" /> Despite lacking a physical form aside from its place as the cave, the vergence was, in its own way, alive.<ref name="Vergence short story">{{StoryCite|story=Vergence (short story)|book=From a Certain Point of View: The Empire Strikes Back}}</ref> [[Jedi Master]] [[Yoda]]'s presence in the [[light side of the Force]] created balance on Dagobah that held back the Cave's influence.<ref name="Light Falls">{{StoryCite|story=The Light That Falls|book=From a Certain Point of View: Return of the Jedi}}</ref>

Because of the cave's dark energy, the area surrounding the cave was permeated with a sense of dread, while [[Force-sensitive]]s often perceived the area as being cold, filled with malice and menace. Despite the negative energy felt by [[Sentience|sentients]], Dagobah's diverse flora and fauna were attracted to the area and flourished. The nature of the vergence's assertion on individuals was highly personal and acted on their worst fears. Apparitions and illusions would materialize in the cave, interacting with the minds of entrants and exploiting their natural weaknesses and worries. The reactions to these apparitions would determine how the illusion played out. The nature of the cave was not simply dark, but a true and sinister evil. The manipulation of the mind was meant to produce the worst outcome for the victim, drawing out the worst reaction and luring them towards the dark side.<ref name="NoP" />

==History==
{{Quote|The cave is power. And darkness. And you will enter.''"<br />"''What's in there?''"<br />"''Only what you've been too weak to bury.|Snoke and Kylo Ren|<ref name="Age of Resistance Snoke">[[Age of Resistance - Supreme Leader Snoke 1|''Age of Resistance - Supreme Leader Snoke'' 1]]</ref>}}
The vergence was visited by Force-sensitives for a [[millennium]] and lost count of how many came into it, although it noted none of its offworld visitors returned.<ref name="Vergence short story" /> Without a powerful force in the light side to balance out the Cave, its power was able to seep out.<ref name="Light Falls" /> During the [[Clone Wars]], and while on a quest to learn the path to [[Immortality|eternal consciousness]], Yoda entered the cave under the guidance of the [[Death|deceased]] [[Jedi Master]] [[Qui-Gon Jinn]]. Inside, Yoda saw a [[dream]]-like [[Force vision|vision]] of the [[Order 66|destruction]] of the [[Jedi Order]] and the [[Sith Lord]] [[Darth Sidious]], a vision that overwhelmed him.<ref name="Voices">{{TCW|Voices}}</ref> Upon casting the vision of Sidious, the vergence wished it had a physical body with which it could kneel before the [[Sith]].<ref name="Vergence short story" />

Following the war, Yoda returned to Dagobah in [[Exile (punishment)|exile]].<ref name="Episode V" /> Much to the surprise of the vergence, Yoda returned to it, marking the first time an offworlder had ever returned to the cave. Yoda visited the vergence every time several [[orbit]]s had passed to face his fears.<ref name="Vergence short story" /> Yoda and the Cave balanced each other out as representatives of the light and dark sides, respectively. Thanks to Yoda, the Cave was not able to exert its influence across Dagobah, and, so, balance existed within the Dagobah ecosystem.<ref name="Light Falls" />

[[File:TrennisYodaDooku-Yoda10.png|thumb|left|250px|Yoda had a vision of Keeve Trennis in the Cave of Evil while fighting an apparition of Dooku.]]
Around [[3 ABY]],<ref name="Yoda 10 date">[[Yoda 10|''Yoda'' 10]] takes place immediately before the [[Battle of Hoth]], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[3 ABY]].</ref> during the [[Galactic Civil War]] and years after Jedi Master [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'s death at the hands of the [[Dark Lord of the Sith]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], Kenobi's [[Force spirit|spirit]] visited Yoda and guided him into the cave to face his fears, in preparation for the arrival of the fledgling [[Jedi]] [[Luke Skywalker]] who would soon come to seek training. Yoda was first met with an apparition of his former student and fallen Jedi [[Dooku]], who confessed to killing Jedi Master [[Yaddle]] and many others, which he blamed on Yoda's failure to see what he had become. More visions, including that of Jedi Masters [[Keeve Trennis]] and [[Mace Windu]], a burning Anakin Skywalker, [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]], and [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]], all appeared around him, blaming him for their deaths. Finally, Darth Sidious, now [[Emperor]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], appeared before him, proclaiming Yoda as the greatest of his apprentices due to the exiled Jedi's blindness towards the fall of the Jedi and [[Galactic Republic|Republic]]. Yoda then remembered back to a lesson learned with a young [[Scalvi]] named [[Bree Menaren]], that failure was the greatest teacher. Letting go of his guilt and fear, he defeated the visions and left the cave, ready to both teach and learn.<ref name="Yoda 10">[[Yoda 10|''Yoda'' 10]]</ref>

[[File:Lukes_vision.png|thumb|Luke Skywalker faces Darth Vader in the Cave, only to find his own face beneath the Dark Lord's mask.]]
During his [[Jedi training|training]] with Master Yoda, Luke Skywalker had to enter the cave as a test. In the hollow, Skywalker had a vision in which he [[Duel on Dagobah (3 ABY)|faced]] Darth Vader. As Skywalker seemed to strike down Vader with a high [[lightsaber]] blow, the illusory [[Sith Lord]]'s [[helmet]]ed head rolled on the floor, and the face shield cracked open to reveal the young Jedi's own countenance behind the mask.<ref name="Episode V" /> As Skywalker departed Dagobah, the vergence realized Yoda had been using it to strengthen himself for years and test Skywalker, additionally feeling a strong word, "[[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Alliance]]," radiate off the young Jedi.<ref name="Vergence short story" />

A few months later, a [[Sava]] named [[The Archivist|Madelin Sun]] arrived on Dagobah in search of Yoda. After saving her from a monster, Yoda used the Force to lead Sun into the cave. While inside, she saw visions which dissuaded her from looking for him. She then left the planet as Yoda watched from afar.<ref name="CR 3">[[Crimson Reign 3|''Crimson Reign'' 3]]</ref> Yoda's death in [[4 ABY]]<ref name="Timelines" /> allowed the Cave of Evil to expand its influence across Dagobah once more, kicking off an era of twilight for the swampy world.<ref name="Light Falls" />

[[File:KyloVsVisionLuke-AORSnoke1.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Kylo Ren battles a vision of Luke Skywalker in the Cave of Evil.]]
Many years after Skywalker was trained by Yoda on Dagobah, his [[Ben Solo|nephew]], now Kylo Ren, would travel here alongside his master [[Snoke]] and go to the Cave of Evil. There he faced visions of Luke and his parents, [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] and [[Han Solo]]. Though able to kill the vision of Luke, Ren was not able to kill the visions of his parents and fooled Snoke by destroying the Cave of Evil. Snoke complained that the cave had stood for thousands of years and that he planned to send other apprentices to it, to which Ren replied that the past is past and that he would not need any other apprentices.<ref name="Age of Resistance Snoke" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Cave of Evil first appeared in the [[1980]] film [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']], the second installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[original trilogy]].<ref name="Episode V" /> In the film, the cave has a corresponding musical theme called "The Training of a Jedi Knight/The Magic Tree," which was composed by [[John Williams]].<ref name="Soundtrack">[[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back Original Soundtrack|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'' Original Soundtrack]]</ref> The cave was first identified as the Cave of Evil in ''The Story of Starkiller'', a documentary for the [[Star Wars Legends|Legends]] [[Star Wars video games|video game]] ''[[Star Wars: The Force Unleashed II]]''.<ref name="Story">{{LucasArts|url=games/theforceunleashed2|text=''Star Wars: The Force Unleashed II''}} {{C|''The Story of Starkiller'' video documentary}}</ref> The name was later [[canon]]ized by the [[2015]] reference book ''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''.<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref>

